  <p>
    This page is the map. It explains which moving parts exist, where requests
    enter, and how the core school entities relate — read it before the other
    System Internals pages.
  </p>

  <h2>Runtime shape</h2>
  <p>
    KoAkademy is a <strong>modular monolith</strong>. One Laravel 12 application
    serves everything — admin panel, portals, public pages, and API — running on
    <strong>PHP 8.5 under Laravel Octane with FrankenPHP</strong> in production.
    The long-running worker means application boot happens once per worker, not
    per request; code must not leak mutable state between requests (Octane-safe
    patterns are expected in contributions).
  </p>
  <p>
    The production container image is a multi-stage build
    (<code>docker/Dockerfile</code>): Composer dependencies → Wayfinder route
    generation → Bun/Vite asset build → a
    <code>dunglas/frankenphp:1.9-php8.5</code> runtime. Supervisord variants in
    the image can run the web worker, queue workers ("station"), scheduler, and
    Pulse processes; alternative nginx/php-fpm, RoadRunner, and Swoole
    configurations ship for operators who need them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Supporting services are external: <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> (primary data),
    <strong>Redis</strong> (cache, sessions, queues), <strong>Gotenberg</strong>
    (PDF rendering), and <strong>S3-compatible object storage</strong> (uploads
    via media library).
  </p>

